</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Results on Image Datasets</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On image datasets, we observe similar results on text datasets. Specifically, we see that KD fall short on distilling the debiasing capabilities. Such ability is transferred more smoothly as teacher and student get similar in scale.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F9" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.26038v1/heatmap_tvs_image.png" id="A5.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:452/112;" width="452" height="112" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9: </span><span id="A5.F9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">C1: Teacher vs. Student</span>: average performance gaps between teacher and student models on ID, OOD, and Spurious Gap across image datasets. X-axis and Y-axis show the scale of student (<math id="A5.F9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>) and teacher (<math id="A5.F9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>) respectively. Each cell shows the performance gap between corresponding scales of a teacher and a student.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A5.F10" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.26038v1/heatmap_kvn_image.png" id="A5.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:452/114;" width="452" height="114" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 10: </span><span id="A5.F10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">C2: Non-KD vs. KD</span>: average performance gaps between Non-KD and KD models on ID, OOD, and Spurious Gap across image datasets. X-axis and Y-axis show the scale of student (<math id="A5.F10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>) and teacher (<math id="A5.F10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>) respectively. Each cell shows the performance gap between corresponding scales of a teacher and a student.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Detailed Results on Debiasing Methods and Backbones</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present the detailed results of individual debiasing method and backbone below.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F11" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.26038v1/cka_kvn.png" id="A6.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:234/92;" width="234" height="92" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span><span id="A6.F11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">C2: KD vs. Non-KD</span>: Centralized Kernel Alignment. Highers values indicate higher similarity. X-axis and Y-axis refer to the layers of KD (<math id="A6.F11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>) and Non-KD (<math id="A6.F11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>) respectively.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A6.F12" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.26038v1/heatmap_per_method_tvs_bert.png" id="A6.F12.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:452/155;" width="452" height="155" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 12: </span><span id="A6.F12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">C1: Teacher vs. Student</span>: average performance gaps between teacher and student models on ID, OOD, and Spurious Gap on BERT.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A6.F13" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.26038v1/heatmap_per_method_tvs_t5.png" id="A6.F13.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:452/155;" width="452" height="155" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 13: </span><span id="A6.F13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">C1: Teacher vs. Student</span>: average performance gaps between teacher and student models on ID, OOD, and Spurious Gap on T5.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A6.F14" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.26038v1/heatmap_per_method_tvs_resnet.png" id="A6.F14.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:452/199;" width="452" height="199" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 14: </span><span id="A6.F14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">C1: Teacher vs. Student</span>: average performance gaps between teacher and student models on ID, OOD, and Spurious Gap on ResNet.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A6.F15" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.26038v1/heatmap_per_method_tvs_vit.png" id="A6.F15.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:452/199;" width="452" height="199" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 15: </span><span id="A6.F15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">C1: Teacher vs. Student</span>: average performance gaps between teacher and student models on ID, OOD, and Spurious Gap on ViT.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A6.F16" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.26038v1/agreement_per_method_tvs_bert.svg" id="A6.F16.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:452/150;" width="452" height="150"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 16: </span><span id="A6.F16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">C1: Teacher vs. Student</span>: prediction agreement on BERT. Left: varying <math id="A6.F16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> (X-axis) given a fixed teacher with <math id="A6.F16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> = L. Right: varying <math id="A6.F16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> (X-axis) given a fixed student with <math id="A6.F16.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> = T. Agreement increases as the scale of teacher and student get closer.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite"><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a></cite><cite class="ltx_cite"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a></cite></p>
</div>
